WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.962 --> 00:00:06.240
Petyr Baelish: From the east coast of the Vale,&nbsp;
the Fingers reach out into the Narrow Sea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.880
four rocky peninsulas plagued by wind and rain,&nbsp;
and barren to all but the hardiest of weeds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:20.160
The ancestral home of House Baelish.
Our house began with my great-grandfather,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:26.160
a Braavosi sellsword who came to the Vale at the&nbsp;
invitation of House Corbray. My grandfather raised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:31.200
himself to the status of hedge knight and even&nbsp;
managed to acquire a bit of land and a keep on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.080
the smallest of the Fingers, though I do believe&nbsp;
he missed sleeping under his titular hedges.
&nbsp;

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.400
The only thing worse than owning&nbsp;
a dreary and desolate land&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:46.240
is owning only a small portion of it. Luckily,&nbsp;
I didn't spend much time there as a child.
&nbsp;

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:52.000
During the War of the Ninepenny Kings&nbsp;
(a cheap name for a cheap cause),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.240
while other men fought for the king, my&nbsp;
father fought to befriend Hoster Tully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.560
Lord Paramount of the Trident and head of one&nbsp;
of the oldest and greatest Houses in Westeros.
&nbsp;

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.680
Thanks to my father's heroic efforts, Lord&nbsp;
Hoster agreed to foster me at Riverrun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:11.040
with his own children. Until then, my&nbsp;
whole world had been a small tower on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:16.080
the gull-stained rocks of the Fingers.
But when I first saw the stone walls of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:22.640
Riverrun rising from the Trident, towering over me&nbsp;
(back then I was a little more easily impressed),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:26.880
the boy in me thought the gods&nbsp;
themselves must live in such a place.
&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:33.600
I soon learned otherwise. Lord Tully's&nbsp;
son, Edmure, was quick to ensure I would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:38.320
never forget myself in their House.
He nicknamed me "Littlefinger," after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:42.320
my size and homeland, and the name&nbsp;
was just cruel enough to stick.
&nbsp;

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:50.480
His sisters, Lysa and Catelyn, made me a pawn in&nbsp;
their kissing-game, traded back and forth between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:57.120
them for practice. Needless to say, I enjoyed&nbsp;
spending time with them more than Edmure. As we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:04.640
grew older, the game began to change, as all games&nbsp;
do. Lysa grew more bold and Cat more demure.
&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:10.160
When Lord Tully announced Cat's betrothal to&nbsp;
a brute from the North, whom she'd never met,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:13.760
I realized her duty would outweigh&nbsp;
any feelings she had for me.
&nbsp;

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:22.320
Fool that I was, I challenged this Brandon Stark&nbsp;
to a duel for her hand. He was a warrior. I was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:27.920
a boy. If Cat had not intervened, he would&nbsp;
have killed me and laughed over my corpse.
&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:35.680
For my insolence, Lord Tully banished me from&nbsp;
Riverrun. No matter. I had learned everything by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:41.680
then. I would fight my battles not with swords,&nbsp;
but with wits, as few men could match me.
&nbsp;

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:49.760
Even then, House Baelish might have died out on&nbsp;
the rocks of the Fingers. I was again a poor lord,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:54.960
with no allies and no prospects except, if he&nbsp;
were lucky, a daughter of a middling merchant.
&nbsp;

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:01.840
Then, opportunity arose. The Mad King executed&nbsp;
that Brandon Stark and incited a rebellion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:08.560
My old "friend," Lysa Tully, was married off&nbsp;
to Jon Arryn, Lord of the Vale, to cement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:13.520
the alliance against the Iron Throne.
Bringing her within my circle again, I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:19.360
quickly capitalized on our former "affection" and&nbsp;
persuaded her to have me appointed as controller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:27.040
of customs at Gulltown, the Vale's greatest port.
Wars burn gold like wildfire. When I increased the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:32.720
port's income tenfold, her husband took notice&nbsp;
of this lowly lord from the Fingers. And when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:37.920
new and profligate King Robert needed a Master of&nbsp;
Coin who could find gold where no one else could,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:45.600
why, Lord Arryn knew just the man.
Sandor Clegane: Honor. Glory. Lies to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.000
make idiot boys want knighthood, and&nbsp;
idiot girls spread their legs for it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:56.800
Let me tell you what makes a knight:&nbsp;
killing. Either enough men, or the right man.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.360
House Clegane should know.&nbsp;
We're very good at both.
&nbsp;

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:07.040
Most families claim some great ancestors so&nbsp;
far back that nobody can prove them liars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:13.440
Not us. My grandfather kept the&nbsp;
kennel for Lord Tytos Lannister&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:20.640
of Casterly Rock, the father of Lord Tywin.&nbsp;
Lord Tytos was a weak man who didn't know it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:28.320
One day while hunting, he stumbled on a lioness.
Instead of embracing the man who wore her on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:34.000
banners, she tried to tear out his throat.
Lucky my grandfather came up with the dogs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:40.480
and drove the big cat away.
As a reward, the Cleganes got lands and a keep and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:45.680
a son to squire for the Lannisters. We took the&nbsp;
three hounds who died for them as our new sigil.
&nbsp;

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:52.560
When Tywin Lannister became Lord of Casterly Rock,&nbsp;
he wanted more from his former kennelmaster than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.560 --> 00:05:00.000
fealty. He bet that training hounds to kill&nbsp;
isn't far from training boys to kill. In just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:05.840
two generations, my brother Gregor and I proved&nbsp;
him right. I gutted my first man at twelve.
&nbsp;

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:13.120
Years after, servants started disappearing in&nbsp;
our keep, and even a sister I don't remember.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:20.400
But nobody could prove anything against&nbsp;
Gregor or dared if they caught him at it.
&nbsp;

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:26.160
For my father wanted a knight in our family&nbsp;
and thought he’d found one in Gregor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:30.800
who at thirteen towered over enough men&nbsp;
that they called him "the Mountain."
&nbsp;

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:34.080
Sure, Gregor looks quite the&nbsp;
champion from a distance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.720
but a mountain can't cleave&nbsp;
a man in half in one blow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:46.400
and won't break a wench's face if she talks.
Through Lord Tywin's influence, Prince Rhaegar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:51.840
Targaryen kindly anointed my brother personally.&nbsp;
A great honor for our family, everyone said.
&nbsp;

00:05:53.200 --> 00:06:00.000
One year later, Ser Gregor chivalrously sacked&nbsp;
the Prince's city, brained the Prince's baby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.240
and murdered the Prince's wife, winning our family&nbsp;
yet more honor from the new king and queen.
&nbsp;

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:13.440
Soon after, my father died,&nbsp;
they say, in a hunting accident.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:20.800
The same day that Gregor became lord of the&nbsp;
Clegane lands, gold, and anything under his roof,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:28.480
I left our home to take service at Casterly Rock.&nbsp;
Lord Tywin is not like his father. Neither is King&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:34.960
Joffrey or the likes of me would never be on&nbsp;
the Kingsguard, with all those "true knights."
&nbsp;

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:40.480
Between them, the man who serves the&nbsp;
Lannisters will never lack for killing.
&nbsp;

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:49.040
I'll guard this king, such as he is. Gregor&nbsp;
will kill the other ones, such as he does.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:55.440
When we're done, we’ll see how many people&nbsp;
still believe in songs and fairytales.
&nbsp;

00:06:55.440 --> 00:07:01.600
Jon Snow:Where House Reed holds the gate to&nbsp;
the North, House Manderly holds the port.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:06.480
White Harbor, the closest thing to a southern&nbsp;
city we have governed by the closest thing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:11.280
a southern family we have. Generations ago, the&nbsp;
Manderlys were driven from the Reach, but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:16.880
Starks gave them their land in return for fealty.
Now White Harbor is the richest city of the North,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:22.640
and the Manderlys the richest family. Not in&nbsp;
gold and silver like their southern counterparts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:27.760
but in fish and grain and trade.
As for the other great Northern houses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:31.360
the Starks brought them into the&nbsp;
fold during the Age of Heroes.
&nbsp;

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:35.760
A Stark wrestled an ironborn for Bear&nbsp;
Island and gave it to the Mormonts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:41.520
A Stark granted a keep and land to a younger son,&nbsp;
Karlon, in return for putting down a rebellion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:44.720
His family then grew up into the Karstarks.
&nbsp;

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:49.040
Starks fought the wildlings and their&nbsp;
Kings-Beyond-the-Wall beside the Umbers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:55.680
of Last Hearth, thus earning their fealty.
Boltons. Back then, they were the bane of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.680 --> 00:08:02.080
North. A few were even rumored to wear their&nbsp;
enemies' flayed skins as cloaks. But after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:08.320
centuries of war, they too bent the knee.
Sansa Stark: Rodrik Stark wrestled an Ironborn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:11.840
lord for Bear Island and granted&nbsp;
it to House Mormont when he won.
&nbsp;

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:16.720
A younger son of our family, Karlon&nbsp;
Stark, won his own keep after he put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:21.040
down a rebellion and founded House Karstark,&nbsp;
one of the most powerful in the North.
&nbsp;

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:26.720
When the Manderlys were exiled from the Reach,&nbsp;
my ancestors shielded them and gave them a home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:31.840
at the mouth of the White Knife in return for&nbsp;
holding the river against pirates and invaders.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.960
Now they're one of the&nbsp;
wealthiest houses in the North.
&nbsp;

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:40.160
I'm not so naive to pretend that the&nbsp;
entire North welcomed Stark rule.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:45.360
The last Warg King was slain at Sea Dragon&nbsp;
Point along with all his sons and beasts.
&nbsp;

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:50.160
The last Marsh King died at the hands of&nbsp;
King Rickard Stark, and House Reed has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:56.160
held the swamps of the Neck ever since. 
Houses Greenwood, Towers, Amber, Frost.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.960 --> 00:09:00.480
None survive today as more&nbsp;
than names in dusty old books.
&nbsp;

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:07.680
But my ancestors never wanted to destroy their&nbsp;
foes root and stem. The Umbers of Last Hearth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:12.000
and the Glovers of Deepwood Motte bent the&nbsp;
knee and became loyal vassals of House Stark.
&nbsp;

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:19.360
The Red Kings of House Bolton wore cloaks made&nbsp;
from the skins of Stark princes they'd flayed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:24.720
and one of the Boltons was even known as the&nbsp;
Redarm because he liked to plunge an arm into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:31.360
the bellies of captive Starks and pull out their&nbsp;
entrails with his bare hand. The North deserved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:38.720
to be wiped clean of them. Yet my ancestors spared&nbsp;
them after their defeat because they believed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:45.760
North couldn't afford to fight itself any longer.
Time soon proved them right. When the Andals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:51.680
swept into Westeros, they obliterated all the&nbsp;
kingdoms of the First Men except the North.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:57.520
Each of the southern kingdoms fought the invaders&nbsp;
on its own, but the North fought as one.
&nbsp;

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:02.640
When the Andals tried to sail on the White&nbsp;
Knife, the Manderlys fell on their ships.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:14.000
When the Andals tried to march an army through&nbsp;
the Neck, the Reeds fell on their soldiers.

